---
import ProjectLayout from '../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import OverviewBar from "../components/overviewBar.astro";
import RedBarLeft from '../components/redBarLeft.astro';
import YellowBarRight from '../components/yellowBarRight.astro';
import ColumnBar from '../components/columnBar.astro';
import LoneStarScreen from "../assets/images/photos/LSSphoto.png";
import Oculus from "../assets/images/photos/oculusPhoto.jpg";
---
<ProjectLayout>
    <main>
        <OverviewBar Title="The Lone Star Saloon">
        <p slot="overview">Lone Star Saloon is a first-person arcade shooter that combines fast-paced action with Tapper-Style bar management gameplay. I was in charge of overall team and project management, as well as developing and integrating the game for Virtual Reality.</p>
        <ul slot="technologies list">
            <li><strong>Programs Used</strong></li>
            <li>-Unity</li>
            <li>-C#</li>
            <li>-Oculus Quest</li>

        </ul>
        <div class="video-wrapper right" slot="content">
                <video controls>
                    <source src="/videos/TheLoneStarSaloonUpdated.mp4" type="video/mp4">
                    Your browser does not support the video tag.
                </video>
            </div>
        </OverviewBar>
        <RedBarLeft Title="Challenges">
            <img src={LoneStarScreen.src} class="video-wrapper left" alt="The Lone Star Saloon Opening Screen" slot="content">
            <div slot="text">
            <p class="white indented-text">This game presented unique challenges in terms of integrating traditional Tapper-style gameplay with Virtual Reality mechanics. I had to carefully design the movement system, object interactions, and overall user experience to ensure that the game felt natural and immersive in VR. Additionally, I had to consider the limitations and capabilities of the Oculus Quest platform to optimize performance and maintain a smooth gameplay experience.</p>
            </div>
        </RedBarLeft>
        <YellowBarRight Title="Virtual Reality Integration">
            <p class="indented-text" slot="text">As a part of this project I was wholly responsible for integrating the game into Virtual Reality, ensuring that all mechanics and interactions worked seamlessly with VR controls and the Oculus Quest platform. This posed a unique challenge in communication, and development of scripts that could handle VR interactions effectively. I had to carefully consider player movement, object interactions, and the overall user experience to make sure the game felt natural and immersive in VR.</p>
            <img src={Oculus.src} class="video-wrapper right" alt="Oculus Quest" slot="content">
        </YellowBarRight>
        <ColumnBar>
            <h4 class="black small centered" slot="title1">Where I Succeeded</h4>
            <p class="centered" slot="text1">This was the first in class project where we were able to organize and pick our team without instructor intervention, which allowed for better collaboration and more efficient project management. The process began with a peer approaching me with an idea and asking me to help them pitch it to others and form a team. From there, we were able to divide responsibilities based on each team member's strengths and expertise, leading to a more streamlined and effective development process.</p>
            <h4 slot="title2" class="black small centered">Where I Can Improve</h4>
            <p slot="text2" class="centered">While the project was successful in many ways, there are areas where I can improve. One key area is in time management and ensuring that all team members are aligned on deadlines and milestones. Additionally, I can work on enhancing my communication skills to better convey ideas and provide constructive feedback throughout the development process.</p>
            <a href="https://mannixgames.itch.io/the-lone-star-saloon" slot="link">
            <u class="black"> You Can Play Lone Star Saloon Here!</u></a>
        </ColumnBar>
    </main> 
</ProjectLayout>